##
## What never reaches the image build.
##
## The name is .dockerignore rather than .containerignore because both runtimes
## read this one. Podman looks for .containerignore first and falls back to
## this, and Docker reads only this.
##

##
## file: local environment
##
## The build is driven by its build arguments, which is how compose points an
## image at a different api. A .env copied in would win over those arguments,
## because the file is the source that wins, and the image would be built for
## whatever this machine happens to be pointed at.
##
.env
.env.*

##
## directory: installed and generated
##
## node_modules in particular. The build installs its own from the lock file,
## and copying the host's over the top replaces binaries built for one platform
## with binaries built for another.
##
node_modules
build
.svelte-kit
.dist
.cache

##
## file: nothing the build reads
##
*.md
.gitignore
.dockerignore
